menu "SENTRY-Node board"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The board target.
#
# One codebase, two targets. The DevKit is the default and must stay the
# default: every gate, runbook and measurement in this repository was taken on
# that board, so a build whose meaning changed the day this menu arrived would
# invalidate all of them at once.
#
# Selecting a board changes ONE thing - which header boards/ hands to
# board_pins.h. It does not change a detector constant, a threshold, a tier
# default or a frame budget, and the no-regression certificate asserts as much
# by proving the DevKit image still passes the golden gate.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
choice SENTRY_BOARD
    prompt "Target board"
    default SENTRY_BOARD_DEVKIT
    help
      Which physical board this image is for. Affects only the pin map and
      the BOARD_HAS_* capability flags in main/boards/; nothing in the
      detection path reads either.

config SENTRY_BOARD_DEVKIT
    bool "ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 on the breadboard (the proven build)"
    help
      The board every measurement in this project was taken on. Four INMP441
      microphones, e-paper, WS2812, buzzer, motor and a snooze button, wired
      on a breadboard. No battery telemetry, no charger, no radio, no slide
      switch. Geometry profile: breadboard_plus_v1 (plus/cross, 40.64 x
      60.96 mm).

config SENTRY_BOARD_PCB_A2
    bool "SENTRY-Node PCB rev A2"
    help
      The custom board. Reuses the DevKit's fourteen proven GPIO numbers
      exactly - zero firmware change - and adds a VBAT sense
      divider, a BQ24074-class charger STAT line, an Ai-Thinker Ra-01H
      (SX1276) LoRa module on the e-paper's SPI2 bus, and a slide switch that
      gates the regulator enable. Geometry profile: pcb_rev_a2 (corner
      square, 56 mm sides).

      Every hardware acceptance for this target is owed.

endchoice

endmenu
